    "bottomLine": "A practical middle ground when 2,000 watts is not quite enough and the iGen4500 is more than you want to spend.",
    "description": "The GP3500iO splits the difference between suitcase inverters and full-size portables. Generac rates it at 3,000 running and 3,500 starting watts, and its PowerRUSH feature is designed to help start motor loads like a sump pump or window air conditioner that a 2,200-watt unit might struggle with. That makes it a reasonable small-house choice for a refrigerator, freezer, sump pump and lights together, if you stagger start-ups. It is an inverter, so output is clean for electronics, and it throttles down at light loads to save fuel. The open frame keeps the cost and weight down compared with an enclosed design, but it also lets more engine noise out, so it is not the one for a narrow side yard against a neighbor's bedroom. COsense shuts it down if carbon monoxide builds. Expect roughly $650 to $900 at the time of writing."
  },
  {
    "id": "westinghouse-igen4500",
